These details are provided solely to identify my records. They must not be used for any other purpose or added to your records.

I REQUEST THAT YOU:
1. Delete all personal data you hold about me from your databases, products and backups in the ordinary course.
2. Stop selling, licensing, sharing or otherwise disclosing my personal data, including for targeted advertising and profiling. I object to any such processing and to all direct marketing.
3. Remove my information from any public-facing listing, search result or people-search page.
4. Pass this request on to every third party, client, partner or service provider to whom you have disclosed my personal data, and tell me who they are.
5. Confirm in writing when this has been done, and tell me which categories of my data you held and where you obtained them.

If you must keep a minimal record (for example my email address on a suppression list) solely to ensure that my data is not collected again, please limit it to what is strictly necessary for that purpose.

Please respond without undue delay and within the deadline set by the law that applies to you: generally one month under the GDPR and UK GDPR, 30 days under the Swiss FADP, and 45 days under the CCPA and most US state laws. If you need more information to verify my identity, please ask only for what is strictly necessary and use it only for verification. Please do not require me to create an account. If you decline any part of this request, please explain why and tell me how I can appeal or complain.

